l sample mean of 2.33%; update by -0.25 pp for easing energy from 11.20% in May to 10.31% in June and by -0.10 pp for food at 0.06%, offset by +0.10 pp for services at 5.10%, rents at 3.38%, and July travel seasonality. Rounded point = 3.20%. The 80% interval uses recent first-print monthly volatility around persistence, widened for July energy/travel swings, giving 2.40% to 4.10%."},{"kind":"text","text":"Upside risk: renewed electricity, gas, motor-fuel, air-ticket, or package-holiday increases could keep the annual rate near May's 4.08% or would land above the interval if they combine with stronger services. Downside risk: another June-like monthly CPI decline, weaker fuel prices, or broader goods discounts could push the print below 2.40% outside the interval."},{"kind":"forecast","point":3.2,"ciLow":2.4,"ciHigh":4.1}]}
